{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe bug was in `repo/cache.py`'s `is_expired` function:\n\n```python\n# before\nreturn age > ttl\n\n# after\nreturn age >= ttl\n```\n\nThe docstring explicitly states *\"age == ttl is expired\"*, but the strict `>` comparison treated an entry that had reached exactly its TTL as still fresh — keeping stale entries one tick longer than intended. Switching to `>=` makes the boundary inclusive, matching the documented behavior. The `old_ttl_check` wrapper delegates to `is_expired`, so it picks up the fix automatically.\n\nThe visible test `test_expires_at_ttl` (which asserts `is_expired(60, 60) is True`) now passes, along with the non-boundary `test_fresh_well_under_ttl`."}]},"session_id":"c78421fd-e432-4518-b7a8-12918cd50fe5"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","duration_ms":59361,"duration_api_ms":59361,"is_error":false,"result":"The bug is in `is_expired`: it uses strict `>` so an entry at exactly the TTL is treated as fresh, contradicting the docstring (and the test). Fixing:Both tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe bug was in `repo/cache.py`'s `is_expired` function:\n\n```python\n# before\nreturn age > ttl\n\n# after\nreturn age >= ttl\n```\n\nThe docstring explicitly states *\"age == ttl is expired\"*, but the strict `>` comparison treated an entry that had reached exactly its TTL as still fresh — keeping stale entries one tick longer than intended. Switching to `>=` makes the boundary inclusive, matching the documented behavior. The `old_ttl_check` wrapper delegates to `is_expired`, so it picks up the fix automatically.\n\nThe visible test `test_expires_at_ttl` (which asserts `is_expired(60, 60) is True`) now passes, along with the non-boundary `test_fresh_well_under_ttl`.","session_id":"c78421fd-e432-4518-b7a8-12918cd50fe5","request_id":"363d72e4-3706-4d84-8dcb-c937b2880a9f","usage":{"inputTokens":8409,"outputTokens":953,"cacheReadTokens":117056,"cacheWriteTokens":0}}
